From 0a98134dd8f0b53dcf5242065d588e4ccf74aa8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ynwang <ynwang@iis.u-tokyo.ac.jp>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:30:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] XSpectra: xepsilon_xyz - x, y and z polarizations of a
 K-edge dipole run together

New &input_xspectra flag xepsilon_xyz (default .false.): the three
Cartesian polarizations are computed in one run (one setup, one S^-1
matrix per k-point) and written as three standard single-polarization
outputs (_x/_y/_z inserted before the extension of x_save_file and
xanes_file). Only for xanes_dipole at s edges; restart and xonly_plot
stop with an error.
- GPU build: lanczos_uspp_acc_batch advances the chains together, h_psi
  and S^-1 act on all active chains at once (one pass over vkb, batched
  FFTs); each chain keeps its own coefficients and convergence test and
  leaves the batch when converged.
- CPU build: the chains run one after the other with the original
  lanczos_uspp (shared setup).
- xanes_dipole generalised to n_lanczos chains; the single-polarization
  path performs the same operations as before.
Small test: Intel CPU single-polarization bit-identical to before, CPU
batch bit-identical to three single runs; GPU single and batch PASS the
phase-2 criteria.
